From a0d521d70370a9f69c85b230c56c6c81f6332f69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:55:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 107/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: hardware overlay plane (LAY1 of
 the UI channel)

Each DE33/v35x channel has four fetch layers ("four overlay layers in
each channel", T527 user manual v0.92, section 5.1), but only LAY0 of
phys 6 was used, so cursor and video always went through the GPU.

Register a DRM overlay plane backed by LAY1 of the same channel:

- per-layer fetch: its own LAY_n block (attctl/mbsize/mbcoor/pitch/laddr)
  with the position relative to the channel window (mbcoor).
- shared registers are composed in sun55i_de_commit() under arm_lock:
  PARA.top_haddr packs one high-address byte per layer (the primary used
  to overwrite the whole register), and the premultiplied bits of every
  attctl follow the visible layers, so a premultiplied layer turns the
  rest to NON_TO_EXC and the mix happens in premultiplied space.
- AFBD/OVL guard: the AFBD replaces the OVL of the whole channel, so
  without a LINEAR LAY0 (AFBC primary or channel off) the compose turns
  any LAY1..3 off.
- overlay atomic_check: LINEAR only, unscaled, and inside the rectangle
  of an unscaled LINEAR primary (the VSU scales the whole channel
  window). The primary check pulls the visible overlays into the commit
  when it switches to AFBC or scaling, so the rejection is atomic.
- immutable zpos: the stacking inside a channel is fixed by the layer
  index.

Disabling or quiescing the channel now turns off all four layers, not
just layer 0.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
